// /etc/lard/greeter.kdl
//
// Minimal niri configuration used as the *host compositor* of the greeter.
// greetd launches: niri --config /etc/lard/greeter.kdl (user greeter).
//
// When the greeter exits (after a successful login, or because it was closed)
// niri must exit too, otherwise greetd keeps waiting for the session process.
// That is why the spawn chains `niri msg action quit` after `lard greeter`.
//
// The binary path is absolute because the greeter user's PATH does not contain
// /usr/local/bin.
//
// Keep this file minimal: niri rejects unknown sections, and old versions are
// common on rolling distributions.

spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "/usr/local/bin/lard greeter; niri msg action quit --skip-confirmation"
